{"type":"record","name":"IbkrPreOpenHeartbeat","namespace":"app.options.ibkr.gex","doc":"The liveness beat for an ARMED surface, under the reserved key __heartbeat|<tradeDate>. The browser FAIL-CLOSES on this: if beats stop past heartbeatDeadlineMs it withholds the window's numbers, and resumes when a beat returns. Its own key means a beat can never compact away the manifest a restart needs. Published to options.ibkr.gex.status.v2 by databento-gex-service's pre-open IBKR GEX publisher (IbkrPreOpenService). The predecessor topic options.ibkr.gex.status carried hand-built JSON strings until 2026-10-17; this record reproduces that JSON FIELD FOR FIELD AND NAME FOR NAME. That is a hard requirement, not tidiness: the feed gateway converts these records to JSON for the browser with AvroJson, which emits exactly the published record's own fields, and option-chain.js reads them BY NAME. Renaming or retyping a field here changes what the browser receives. The registry subject is this record's FULL NAME, under RecordNameStrategy. That is deliberate and not the Confluent default, and here it is load-bearing rather than merely conventional: this ONE topic carries nine distinct value shapes, and a topic-name subject could not hold nine schemas. It also keeps one subject across environments, where TopicNameStrategy would mint a different subject per environment because the topic name carries the environment's TOPIC_PREFIX.","fields":[{"name":"emitterEpoch","type":"long","doc":"The output generation of the emitting session."},{"name":"seq","type":"long","doc":"Monotonic beat sequence, so a consumer can order beats and spot a gap."},{"name":"state","type":"string","doc":"The path state at the moment of the beat. Drawn from the PATH vocabulary — today the producer copies its mutable pathState field into this as a plain string, and the sealed carrier closes that by taking the path-state enum instead. A STRING, not an Avro enum. The strike plane, the path plane and the generation control each draw from a different vocabulary, so one shared enum would have to be the union of all three and would assert less, not more; and a new state would be unreadable to every consumer compiled against the old schema rather than merely unrecognised. The vocabulary is instead closed on the PRODUCER side: each record is built only through its sealed carrier, whose constructor takes the corresponding Java enum, so an unlisted state is unrepresentable at the publication boundary."},{"name":"effectiveTimeMs","type":"long","doc":"When the beat was emitted, in epoch milliseconds. Read by name by the browser's fail-close timer. The browser anchors its server clock from the first present of serverTimeMs, eventTimeMs, atMs, effectiveTimeMs, so this field's NAME is part of the contract."},{"name":"heartbeatDeadlineMs","type":"long","doc":"The deadline past which a missing beat fail-closes the surface. Read by name by the browser; renaming it would silently disable the fail-close."},{"name":"tradeDate","type":"string","doc":"The trade date this beat belongs to."},{"name":"fenceMs","type":"long","doc":"The session's freeze fence, in epoch milliseconds."},{"name":"sessionId","type":"string","doc":"Publishing session identity."}]}